Methylene blue (MB) solution at 50 mg/L was prepared by dissolving methylene blue in deionised water. Then 50 mg of adsorbent was mixed with 200 mL of MB solution and stirred at 200 rpm for 20 min at room temperature. The concentration of MB solution was determined at different contact times by extracting 3 ml of the solution for every 5 min intervals. The effect of adsorbent weight and initial concentration of MB solution were observed using different adsorbent weights (5,10,25, 50, 70 mg) while the initial MB concentration was varied at 10, 20, 50, 100, mg/L. The concentration of MB was determined using UV spectrophotometer (Shimadzu-230PI). The maximum absorption wavelength of methylene blue was recorded at 664 nm. The adsorption capacity of methylene blue on silica sample is calculated using the following equation:1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
